ar tissue","k":"b"},{"i":"nc0e740cd59","c":"6","t":"Thallophyta","f":"Agar","b":"red algae; Ulva — food","k":"b"},{"i":"n2ed1dfebe8","c":"6","t":"Bryophyta","f":"Amphibians of the plant kingdom","b":"need water","k":"b"},{"i":"n2b58a030fa","c":"6","t":"Bryophyta","f":"Moss: gametophyte dominant; protonema; sporophyte","b":"stalk + capsule on the female gametophyte","k":"b"},{"i":"n3910ca3f42","c":"6","t":"Pteridophyta","f":"Sporophyte (2n) dominant; gametophyte","b":"prothallus (n)","k":"b"},{"i":"nb875b3cf2f","c":"6","t":"Pteridophyta","f":"Antheridia","b":"sperm; archegonia — egg","k":"b"},{"i":"n57f2c44aa3","c":"6","t":"Pteridophyta","f":"Homosporous","b":"Psilotum; heterosporous — Selaginella (micro- and megaspores)","k":"b"},{"i":"nddcc1f8c27","c":"6","t":"Gymnosperms and angiosperms","f":"Gymnosperms","b":"naked seeds in cones; conifers, cycads, ginkgoes; Cycas, Pinus, Ephedra; bristlecone pine = oldest living organism","k":"b"},{"i":"n9b36dedbd0","c":"6","t":"Gymnosperms and angiosperms","f":"Angiosperms","b":"flowering; seeds in fruits; most plants on Earth; monocots and dicots; Wolffia ~0.1 cm, Eucalyptus ~100 m","k":"b"},{"i":"n96cf56b02a","c":"6","t":"Monocot vs dicot","f":"Monocot","b":"1 cotyledon, parallel veins, adventitious roots, floral parts in 3s, scattered bundles, 1-pore pollen","k":"b"},{"i":"n3c83f1939c","c":"6","t":"Monocot vs dicot","f":"Dicot","b":"2 cotyledons, netted veins, taproot, floral parts in 4s or 5s, bundles in a ring, 3-pore pollen","k":"b"}]}